# What has to be true of every commit here, cheapest first.
#
# The whole hook is ~4s. That is affordable per commit and is bought back the
# first time it catches a rule that stopped holding, because the alternative is
# finding out from the extension misbehaving in the browser.
#
# Escape hatches: `git commit --no-verify` skips all of it, `SKIP_BUMP=1` keeps
# the checks and leaves the version alone.
#
# One caveat worth knowing: typecheck and the check suites read the *working
# tree*, not the staged content. With unstaged changes in flight they answer a
# slightly different question than "is this commit sound".

npx lint-staged

npm run --silent typecheck
npm run --silent check:all

node scripts/bump-version.mjs
